    {"id": "stone-ladder", "first": "PS", "opens": "CoS", "kind": "ladder, iron rungs set in the shaft's east face, then two iron stiles to the pit's floor", "rooms": ["stone-bay", "stone-pit"], "rect": [150.4, 54.6, 151.6, 55.8], "from": -9.4, "to": 15.6, "face": "east", "within": 0.16, "rungs": {"every": 0.3, "w": 0.6, "stiles": [151.52, 54.88, 151.52, 55.52], "plate": [151.38, 54.8, 151.66, 55.6]}, "state": "proposed", "about": "the way down and back up the shaft (Godric's Snare-and-Lumos answer on architect-stone-rungs-1022, 1.38 pm; option 1 on architect-stone-ladder-1022, taken by the away rule 2.50 pm, 22 October 2026, provisional, Godric to confirm): rungs every 0.3 set in the shaft's east face (x 151.6) from the trapdoor (+15.6) down to the shaft's foot at the pit's roof (-5.9), then on down two iron stiles hung from the shaft's lip to the pit's floor (-9.4), a foot plate pinned to the flags; all within 0.16 of that face, so the jump down the middle keeps about 1.0 by 1.2 clear. Down by the jump onto the Snare; up by the rungs. The Snare grows over them and draws back from his lit wand (Events' stone-chambers.json, req 935; Magic's 931). From the Chamber's year on, as the chambers. v157, ledger 222", "cite": "PS 16"},
    {"id": "feast-loft-ladder", "first": "PS", "kind": "ladder stair, steep, railed, up through a hatch into the loft", "rooms": ["feast-ladder-well", "feast-loft"], "rect": [113.8, 64.0, 114.7, 65.9], "from": 36.4, "to": 41.6, "treads": 18, "rise": 0.29, "state": "designed", "about": "its line the Architect's (ledger line 88); the layout keeps it from u's fill on 7; v37; v38 (ledger line 89 a): it climbs north, its foot at the slot's south end (y 64.0), its head at the hatch's north end (y 65.9), so he comes up facing the round window and the loft's longer part, and steps off west onto the walkway there (feast-loft-hatch-rail); designed on Godric's 1 (architect-v38-1015, taken 11.24 pm on Fawkes's agreement, provisional, Godric to confirm)", "cite": "", "up": [0, 1]},
    {"id": "dovecote-stair", "first": "PS", "kind": "mural stair, curving, narrow, in the south-east drum's wall round its north quarter", "rooms": ["orrery-room", "dovecote"], "arc": {"c": [160.0, 0.0], "r_in": 5.25, "r_out": 6.05, "bearings": [330, 60]}, "from": 26.0, "to": 31.2, "treads": 26, "rise": 0.2, "going": 0.34, "about": "H48's way: from a low arch at bearing 330 on 5 (orrery-stair-arch) clockwise through north to another at 60 on 6 (dovecote-stair-arch), 0.8 wide in the drum's 1.5 of wall (0.25 left inside, 0.45 outside), 26 risers of 0.2, going 0.34 on its line (r 5.65), clear of the loops (south and east) and of the turret's bite (210 to 239); no rect, so the layout's fill and cuts leave it to the tower's square. The staircases tally's open list (ours). Ledger line 101 (req 551; H48); v39, designed on Godric's 1 (architect-v39-1015, taken 11.58 pm on Fawkes's agreement, provisional, Godric to confirm)", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "gallery-flight-east", "first": "PS", "kind": "straight flight, 4 treads, 0.9 wide, down from the gun room's arch", "rooms": ["listeners-gallery"], "span": [[73.4, 85.95], [74.4, 86.85]], "up": [1, 0], "from": 0.0, "to": 0.8, "treads": 4, "about": "H42's four risers from the gun room (-3.0) to the gallery (-3.8), in the gallery's first 1.0 (x 73.4 to 74.4), goings 0.25, its top tread level with the arch's floor; the head 1.8 over every tread (see listeners-gallery); ledger line 102 (req 553, Interiors' docs/interiors/hidden-ways-batch-7.md, Asked); v39, designed on Godric's 1 (architect-v39-1015, taken 11.58 pm on Fawkes's agreement, provisional, Godric to confirm)", "state": "designed", "cite": ""},
    {"id": "gallery-flight-west", "first": "PS", "kind": "straight flight, 6 treads and a riser at the face, 0.9 wide, up into the flanker", "rooms": ["listeners-gallery"], "span": [[44.8, 85.95], [46.3, 86.85]], "up": [-1, 0], "from": 0.0, "to": 1.2, "treads": 6, "about": "H42's seven risers from the gallery (-3.8) to the flanker (-2.4): six treads of 0.25 from x 46.3 (0.3 in the gallery) through the spur's arch to its inner face (x 44.8), the seventh riser there onto the flanker's floor, clear of its gun bed (to y 85.4); the head 1.8 over every nosing (see listeners-gallery and flanker-arch); ledger line 102 (req 553, Interiors' docs/interiors/hidden-ways-batch-7.md, Asked); v39, designed on Godric's 1 (architect-v39-1015, taken 11.58 pm on Fawkes's agreement, provisional, Godric to confirm)", "state": "designed", "cite": ""}
